# EPIC-04 STORY-01: the launcher of tools/build_gemdrive.sh from the GEMDOS drive. GOS's file
# requests (file_io: Dsetpath, Fopen, Fseek, Fread, Fclose) go to Hatari's GEMDOS drive by name,
# through gd_forward, where PP's driver would have read sectors (reference-first-level.exp). The
# names are the game's, in its own case, each part cut to 8.3 by gd_forward: LS2DD asks for
# "dmalogo.imgg", which GEMDOS cuts and the Multidevice's GEMDRIVE does not. Then the title, and a
# click on "1 PLAYER" as in the reference, and the level's own files, which the game loads only if
# it survives level020's load (gd_quiet; EPIC-04 STORY-02).
expect start-tos Pexec\(0, "C:\\LEMMINGS\\START\.TOS"
expect pch Fopen\("LEMMINGS\.PCH"
expect ls2dd Fopen\("LS2DD\.FIC"
expect files-dir Dsetpath\("FILES"\)
expect psyglogo (?i)Fopen\("psyglogo
expect dmalogo (?i)Fopen\("dmalogo\.img"
expect intropar (?i)Fopen\("intropar
expect code-file (?i)Fopen\("code"
expect leveldat (?i)Fopen\("leveldat
quiet title 4
shot title
mouse 70 150
sleep 0.5
event doubleclick
expect level-020 (?i)Fopen\("level020
expect level-files (?i)Fopen\("ground1"
sleep 3
shot preview
